#original-page(595.32pt, 842.04pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 14.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 86.76pt, "Multi-Wavelength transparent Microfluidics for UV–Vis spectroscopy/ X-ray ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.82pt, "Scattering studies of Photoactive Systems ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 129.26pt, "Benedetta Marmiroli,")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(168.5pt, 125.3pt, "a")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(171.86pt, 129.26pt, " Sumea Klokic,")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(236.21pt, 125.3pt, "a")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(239.45pt, 129.26pt, " Barbara Sartori, ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(314.83pt, 125.3pt, "a")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(318.19pt, 129.26pt, " Marie Reißenbüchel, ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(416.02pt, 125.3pt, "a ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(420.94pt, 129.26pt, "Alessio Turchet, ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(494.5pt, 125.3pt, "b")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(498.22pt, 129.26pt, " and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 141.26pt, "Heinz Amenitsch")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(146.9pt, 137.3pt, "a ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 163.22pt, "a Institute of Inorganic Chemistry, Graz University of Technology, Stremayrgasse 9/IV, 8010, Graz, Austria ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 175.22pt, "b Elettra-Sincrotrone Trieste, SS 14 Km 163,5, AREA Science Park, 34149, Basovizza, (Trieste), Italy ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 199.22pt, "Microfluidic devices are increasingly used in synchrotron-based experiments to deliver and probe liquid samples, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 211.46pt, "offering advantages such as minimal sample consumption and reduced radiation damage. Despite their growing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 223.58pt, "use, few devices have been specifically designed for monitoring liquids under photoexcitation, a promising ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 235.82pt, "approach for fast structural transitions. Here, a microfluidic device that is transparent to X-rays in one direction ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 248.06pt, "and simultaneously transmits UV and visible light in the perpendicular direction is presented. The device is ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 260.3pt, "fabricated using lamination and UV lithography on a dry-film resist, eliminating the need for cleanroom facilities ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 272.42pt, "and simplifying production. Its multi-wavelength transparency was validated through UV–Vis spectroscopy, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 284.69pt, "where photoexcitation at different wavelengths induced reversible ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(353.47pt, 284.69pt, "trans–to-cis")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(401.23pt, 284.69pt, " isomerization of azobenzene ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 296.93pt, "and fluoro-azobenzene. X-ray transparency was validated through small-angle X-ray scattering (SAXS) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 309.05pt, "measurements on hemoglobin and CO-ligated hemoglobin sensitive to quaternary structural changes. These ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 321.29pt, "results confirm the suitability of the device for resolving protein structures and photoinduced conformational ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 333.53pt, "dynamics. The design further supports, as some proof-of-concept results show, temperature-jump (T-jump) and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 345.77pt, "time-resolved pump–probe experiments, providing a versatile platform for studying structural evolution in liquid ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 358.01pt, "samples using synchrotron SAXS.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 391.97pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 408.77pt, "Light responsive materials are gaining increasing attention, and have been applied across a wide range ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 421.01pt, "of natural science disciplines. Upon exposure to light, photoactive molecules and supramolecular ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 433.25pt, "assemblies can undergo reversible structural changes altering properties such as geometry, polarity, or ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 445.37pt, "flexibility.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.62pt, 441.89pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.1pt, 445.37pt, " Light is a particularly attractive stimulus for controlling biological functions, as its intensity ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 457.61pt, "and wavelength can be precisely regulated, enabling non-invasive, localized activation with micrometer-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 469.87pt, "scale spatial resolution.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(173.81pt, 466.39pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(177.29pt, 469.87pt, " A well-known example is the photoactive molecule retinal, which enables vision ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 481.99pt, "in mammals through a light-induced conformational change; this has inspired the development of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 494.23pt, "artificial systems such as photoreversible DNA and protein binding.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(365.23pt, 490.75pt, "3,4")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(373.99pt, 494.23pt, " Incorporating photoactive groups ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 506.47pt, "into biomolecules has become an effective strategy to modulate biological activity, as demonstrated by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 518.71pt, "photoactivated drugs that exhibit light-controlled enzyme activity")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(372.43pt, 518.71pt, ",")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(374.95pt, 515.23pt, "1,5")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(387.43pt, 518.71pt, "receptor affinity,")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(463.42pt, 515.23pt, "6")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(467.02pt, 518.71pt, " or targeted ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 530.83pt, "antibiotic action.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(145.22pt, 527.35pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(148.7pt, 530.83pt, " Among these photoactive groups, those that undergo photoisomerization such as azo-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 543.07pt, "groups, commonly referred to as photoswitches, are among the most extensively studied.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(467.86pt, 539.59pt, "7–10")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(482.02pt, 543.07pt, "  Because ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 555.31pt, "light offers excellent spatiotemporal resolution, it is a highly advantageous stimulus for probing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 567.55pt, "photoinduced structural dynamics. Investigating the dynamics during photoexcitation of proteins such ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 579.67pt, "as Rhodopsin")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(129.86pt, 576.19pt, "11")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(137.06pt, 579.67pt, " and CO-ligated hemoglobin")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(257.69pt, 576.19pt, "12")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(264.89pt, 579.67pt, " (HbCO), or of lipids specially tailored for optopharmacology ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 591.91pt, "(the use of light to control drug activity), ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(254.93pt, 588.43pt, "10 ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(263.93pt, 591.91pt, "is crucial for understanding the timescales of light-induced ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 604.15pt, "processes.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(117.86pt, 600.67pt, "13")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(124.94pt, 604.15pt, " Several structural investigations have already been conducted using techniques based on ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 616.27pt, "X-rays, generated by high brilliance synchrotron radiation sources, particularly  X-ray Diffraction, Wide ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 628.51pt, "Angle X-ray Scattering (WAXS), and Small Angle X-ray Scattering (SAXS). ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(382.87pt, 625.03pt, "8,14–19")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(405.91pt, 628.51pt, " Among these, synchrotron ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 640.75pt, "SAXS is widely used in structural biology for nanostructural characterization (typically in the 1-100 nm ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 652.99pt, "range). These techniques are particularly suitable for time resolved measurements, as demonstrated by ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 665.14pt, "Cammarata ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(125.66pt, 665.14pt, "et al.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(147.86pt, 665.14pt, ", who used time-resolved WAXS on hemoglobin (Hb) to reveal coordinated molecular ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 677.38pt, "motions during carbon monoxide (CO) binding and photodissociation.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(381.43pt, 673.9pt, "12")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(388.63pt, 677.38pt, " Such insights are essential for ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 689.62pt, "understanding the transition pathway from excitation to subsequent structural dynamics, and highlight ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 701.86pt, "the increasing use of photosensitive proteins as model systems to investigate inter- and intramolecular ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 713.98pt, "motions that are fundamental to biological and medical processes.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(364.15pt, 710.5pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 726.22pt, "However, such investigations remain challenging mainly due to the constraints imposed on suitable ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 738.46pt, "sample holders. In strongly absorbing samples, light penetration is limited, so the illuminated volume ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 750.576pt, "must be comparable to or smaller than the optical attenuation length.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(382.75pt, 747.096pt, "21")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(389.83pt, 750.576pt, " Microfluidic channels address ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 762.816pt, "this issue effectively, as their geometry can be precisely designed to achieve sample depths on the order ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 775.056pt, "of the optical penetration length, ensuring uniform excitation of the entire sample volume. For protein ")
]

// arXiv source page 2
#original-page(595.32pt, 842.04pt, (image("graphics/page-02.png", width: 4pt), 232.5pt, 694.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 81.6pt, "samples in particular, microfluidic devices have become increasingly popular,")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(417.46pt, 78.12pt, "22,23 ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(435.58pt, 81.6pt, "offering several key ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 93.74pt, "advantages: low sample consumption (critical for scarce protein systems), precise control of diffusion ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 105.98pt, "within microchannels (enabling rapid and accurate mixing), and efficient heat transfer due to their high ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 118.22pt, "surface-to-volume ratio, making them ideal for studying sensitive biological processes. Microfluidic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 130.46pt, "devices also maximize the efficiency of synchrotron-based X-ray experiments on solutions, especially ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 142.58pt, "SAXS, and provide a platform to extend their use to light-responsive samples. They can be employed for ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 154.82pt, "manipulating and delivering the liquid samples.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(304.15pt, 151.34pt, "24–26")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(321.79pt, 154.82pt, " Beyond the aforementioned advantages, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 167.06pt, "microfluidic devices connected to pumps continuously refresh the liquid sample in front of the X-rays ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 179.3pt, "beam, mitigating radiation damage effects provoked by its high intensity. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(432.58pt, 175.82pt, "27")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(439.66pt, 179.3pt, " Although several ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 191.42pt, "microfluidic devices have been reported for light manipulation of samples, only a limited number allow ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 203.66pt, "multi-wavelength transparency.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 215.9pt, "In the past, a square capillary (0.1 x 0.1 mm) was connected to two reservoirs and used for manipulating ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 228.02pt, "starch granules with optical tweezers, while simultaneously measuring their structure with SAXS. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(507.46pt, 224.54pt, "28,29")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 240.26pt, "However, the size of the device was not scalable and was limited to microfocus beamlines, where the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 252.5pt, "dimension of the X-ray beam is smaller than the dimension of the channel, to avoid refraction effects ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 264.74pt, "due to the channel walls. A similar approach was later used to combine optical tweezers with X-ray ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 276.86pt, "fluorescence.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(130.7pt, 273.38pt, "30")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(137.78pt, 276.86pt, " More recently, a microfluidic device with a sample mixer was reported that allows ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 289.13pt, "spatially separated, yet continuous SAXS and UV-Vis monitoring, based on careful material selection for ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 301.37pt, "UV and X-ray transparency.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(191.93pt, 297.89pt, "31  ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 323.57pt, "The material selection and the definition of a suitable fabrication process are tackled in this work, where ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 335.81pt, "an all-polymer microfluidic device tailored for photoexcitation/X-ray experiments is presented.  A ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 347.93pt, "schematic of the device and materials is shown in Figure 1(a).  To achieve transparency to X-rays in one ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 360.17pt, "direction and to UV and visible light in the perpendicular direction, SUEX and IM-PMMA were selected. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 372.41pt, "The microchannel was fabricated by a sequence of lamination and optical lithography steps, with the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 384.53pt, "detailed protocol outlined in this work. While SUEX has already been employed for microfluidic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 396.77pt, "circuits,")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(105.98pt, 393.29pt, "32,33 ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(123.5pt, 396.77pt, " to our knowledge it has never been used with SAXS. The transparency of the device to light ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 409.01pt, "at 365 nm, 450 nm and 513 nm wavelength was tested by photoisomerization of fluoro-azobenzene and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 421.25pt, "azobenzene using UV-Vis spectroscopy, while its X-ray transparency was evaluated studying Hb and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 433.37pt, "HbCO protein solutions using synchrotron SAXS. Based on previous photoexcitation studies in capillaries ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 445.61pt, "for HbCO, the microfluidic channel depth was designed to be below the UV light attenuation length. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 457.85pt, "These results show the proof of principle for the performance of the microfluidic device, demonstrating ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 470.11pt, "its suitability to study a broad range of photosensitive samples using different experimental techniques. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 494.23pt, "Experimental ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.373pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 510.91pt, "Fabrication process")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.38pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(167.54pt, 510.91pt, ".  ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 522.91pt, "The selected geometry of the device is the following: a single channel 1 mm wide, 40 mm long (15 mm ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 535.15pt, "in the X-rays accessible part) and 0.25 mm deep. The thickness of the device walls in the X-rays accessible ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 547.27pt, "part is 0.5 mm. The materials employed for the device and the shape of the channel are shown in the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 559.51pt, "exploded scheme of Figure 1(a), while an outline of the fabrication process of the microchannel can be ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 571.75pt, "found in Figure 1(b).  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 583.99pt, "The fabrication process is considered green as it is based on the dry film SUEX,")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(413.86pt, 580.51pt, "34")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(420.94pt, 583.99pt, " and it does not require ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 596.11pt, "a clean room facility. It can be described in the following steps: ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 618.07pt, "a)")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 618.07pt, "Cutting of an Impact Modified 125 µm IM-PMMA sheet (Goodfellow Cambridge Ltd, UK) and ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 630.31pt, "drilling of two 1 mm diameter holes in order to add the tubing for feeding the channel in a later ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 642.55pt, "stage (see step e). The shape of the IM-PMMA was chosen to ensure an unobstructed path for ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 654.82pt, "the scattered photons (Figure1(b) step a). ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 676.78pt, "b)")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 676.78pt, "Lamination of 250 µm thick SUEX photosensitive resist (micro resist technology GmbH, ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 688.9pt, "Germany) on IM-PMMA. The sample is put on a thin aluminium slide between two 400 µm thick ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 701.62pt, "spacers and laminated at 60")
  #line-at(236.81pt, 701.62pt, "C for three times, in order to ensure the adhesion of the SUEX to ")
  #line-at(108.02pt, 713.86pt, "IM-PMMA, using the rolling mill system Falcon K (BlackHole Lab, France) (Figure 1(b) step b). ")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 735.82pt, "c)")
