  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 411.05pt, "Photoexcitation experiments were performed in combination with time-resolved SAXS measurements ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 423.17pt, "using the optical on-line table available at the Austrian SAXS beamline.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(381.55pt, 419.69pt, "42")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(388.63pt, 423.17pt, " A schematic representation of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 435.41pt, "the experimental set-up showing the laser, the X-ray detectors, and the microfluidic circuit connected ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 447.65pt, "to a syringe pump is shown in Figure 3(a). The microfluidic channel was positioned on the sample holder ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 459.77pt, "with the UV-transparent polymer IM-PMMA oriented towards the incoming laser light (513 nm), which ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 472.03pt, "was transferred to the sample by motorized optical mirrors and lenses.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(382.15pt, 468.55pt, "42")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(389.23pt, 472.03pt, " The light to initiate the photo-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 484.27pt, "switch was delivered by the Yb:KGW femtosecond laser (PHAROS, Light Conversion, Lithuania), which ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 496.51pt, "allows to precisely control the photon-flux and thus the photoresponse of the sample in liquid. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 508.63pt, "Photoexcitation experiments were conducted at increasing photon flux by adjusting the laser ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 520.87pt, "transmission T. Three different values were used: T=5%, 50% and 100%, corresponding to power P ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 533.11pt, "values of P=2.6 mW, 62 mW and 182 mW, respectively. The laser spot size was set with 3.5 mm FWHM.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 545.35pt, "SAXS measurements were conducted on human hemoglobin (Hb). To evaluate the scattering signal of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 557.47pt, "the protein in the microchannel when compared to a standard capillary, a protein solution and the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 569.71pt, "related buffer were measured for 10 s using either a quartz capillary of 1.5 mm of diameter, or the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 581.95pt, "microfluidic device connected to a syringe pump (TSE System GmbH, Germany) infusing with a flow rate ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 594.07pt, "of 0.25 µl/min. As proof of principle of the performance of the microfluidic device under pump probe ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 606.31pt, "conditions, SAXS measurements were performed to study the structure of Hb stabilized by the presence ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 618.55pt, "of the ligand CO (HbCO) before and after green laser irradiation, as reported previously in the study of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 630.79pt, "Cammarata et al. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(149.78pt, 627.31pt, "43")
]

