  #line-at(72.024pt, 522.31pt, "(ΔA = 0.16). After 450 nm illumination, the 8F-AZB in the channel undergoes a shift in the absorption ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 534.55pt, "band of 9 nm, while only of 4 nm in the cuvette. This difference arises from the smaller photoexcited ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 546.67pt, "volume (1.25 μL) and optical path length (0.25 mm) within the microfluidic device, as opposed to the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 558.91pt, "larger volume (100 μL) and 1 mm path length in the cuvette. In the cuvette, only a limited fraction of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 571.15pt, "the liquid is effectively photoexcited, whereas the microchannel design maximizes optical penetration ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 583.39pt, "and excitation efficiency. These results confirm that the microfluidic device enables efficient ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 595.51pt, "photoexcitation using both UV and visible light, demonstrating effective light penetration and optical ")
