  #line-at(72.024pt, 105.98pt, "(light blue dashed with dots line) with corresponding fit (continuous blue line) in the microchannel. The ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 118.22pt, "scattering curve is an average of 40 measurements of 0.1 s.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 142.58pt, "To evaluate the device performance under photoexcitation conditions, static SAXS measurements for ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 154.82pt, "HbCO were first acquired without illumination (light OFF), followed by measurements under continuous ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 167.06pt, "laser irradiation (light ON). The scattering curves were compared. For laser powers of P= 2.6 mW and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 179.3pt, "P=62 mW, subtraction of the light OFF from the light ON curve yielded difference curves oscillating ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 191.42pt, "around zero (Figure S4 of the supplementary information), confirming that illumination did not cause ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 203.66pt, "photodamage.  In contrast, higher laser power (P= 182mW) induced sample damage, as shown in Figure ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 215.9pt, "S5, even flowing the sample at 100 µL/min, which corresponds to a residence time of about 0.5 s under ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 228.02pt, "irradiation. Notably, whenever the protein is damaged, it usually adheres to the walls of the container, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 240.26pt, "be it a standard capillary or a microchannel. In this work, the microchannel was routinely cleaned after ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 252.5pt, "every protein measurement by flowing a 1% v/v aqueous solution of Hellmanex III, followed by rinsing ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 264.74pt, "with Milli-Q water. Owing to the chemical resistance of SUEX, the device can be efficiently cleaned and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 276.86pt, "reused multiple times. The scattering curves of the buffer inside the microchannel before and after ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 289.13pt, "cleaning are shown in Figure S6.")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 301.37pt, "Photo-illumination experiments were conducted by continuously acquiring SAXS images of 0.1 s ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 313.61pt, "exposure time first with light off, and then switching it on and measuring the changes. Three laser power ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 325.73pt, "values were employed (P= 2.6 mW, 62 mW and 182 mW). Both the photosensitive protein HbCO and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 337.97pt, "the buffer solution were flowing in the microchannel at 100 µl/min. For completeness, the empty ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 350.21pt, "microchannel was also measured. From each dataset, the invariant and the correlation length were ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 362.33pt, "determined and plotted as a function of measurement time. The invariant is shown in Figure 6 (a) for ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 374.57pt, "protein and (b) for buffer and empty device, while the correlation length is reported in Figure S7 (a) for ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 386.81pt, "protein and (b) for buffer and empty device. The correlation length remained constant for protein, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 399.05pt, "buffer and empty device at P= 2.6 mW and 62 mW. At P=182 mW, a clear change in the correlation ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 411.17pt, "length is observed only for the protein, while the buffer, after an initial variation, returns to its pre-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 423.41pt, "irradiation value. As the correlation length is related to the characteristic dimensions of the protein, ")
