  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 81.6pt, "When considering the invariant versus time, no changes are observed at P= 2.6 mW. At 62 mW and 182 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 93.74pt, "mW, however, switching on the light produces a pronounced signal jump, that increases with the laser ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 105.98pt, "power. This effect is observed for both the protein and the buffer, and is also detectable in the empty ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 118.22pt, "channel. This behavior is attributed to laser induced thermocapillary effect, ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(410.26pt, 114.74pt, "27")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(417.34pt, 118.22pt, " where energy from the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 130.46pt, "laser heats the microchannel and the sample, resulting in a thermal signal that overlaps with the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 142.58pt, "scattering signature of protein structural changes. A similar effect was reported by Cammarata et al., ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.707pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(516.22pt, 139.1pt, "43")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 10.302pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 154.82pt, "who suggested decoupling heating and photolysis contributions by subtracting, at each time delay in a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 167.06pt, "pump-probe experiment, the signal taken after photolysis recovery but before thermal relaxation (for ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 179.3pt, "HbCO this occurs within 32 ms). The magnitude of the thermal jump increases with laser power, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 191.42pt, "indicating that the microchannel could, in principle, be used for temperature-jump (T-jump) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 203.66pt, "experiments. In such applications, the contribution of the channel itself must be considered, and the T-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 215.9pt, "jump can be calibrated by measuring samples with known structural transitions at defined ")
